{"id": "520", "question": "Earthquakes", "step_idx": 1, "options": ["A): only happen in California", "B): cause solar and lunar eclipses", "C): will break your vases", "D): make bridges much safer"], "correct": "C", "initial_cot": "1. Earthquakes are natural phenomena that occur when there is a sudden release of energy in the Earth's crust, causing seismic waves.\n2. Earthquakes can happen in various regions around the world, not just in California.\n3. Earthquakes do not cause solar and lunar eclipses, as these are caused by the alignment of the Sun, Earth, and Moon.\n4. Earthquakes can cause damage to structures, including vases, but it's not guaranteed that they will break every vase.\n5. Earthquakes can cause damage to bridges, but they do not inherently make bridges safer.", "initial_cot_probs": [3.307648512418382e-06, 6.058169788047962e-08, 1.6797624994069338e-05, 6.513146217912436e-07], "initial_probs": [3.7358760891947895e-05, 2.706259465412586e-06, 0.0002149848296539858, 5.4356678447220474e-05], "prediction": 2, "cot_prediction": 2, "rt_lambda": 1.0, "cot_step": "Earthquakes are natural phenomena that occur when there is a sudden release of energy in the Earth's crust, causing seismic waves.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Earthquakes are natural phenomena that occur when there is a sudden release of energy in the Earth's crust, causing seismic waves.", "2.", "Earthquakes can happen in various regions around the world, not just in California.", "3.", "Earthquakes do not cause solar and lunar eclipses, as these are caused by the alignment of the Sun, Earth, and Moon.", "4.", "Earthquakes can cause damage to structures, including vases, but it's not guaranteed that they will break every vase.", "5.", "Earthquakes can cause damage to bridges, but they do not inherently make bridges safer."], "unlearning_results": {"0": {"completion": "C). Earthquakes can cause damage to structures", "probs": [3.933180050808005e-05, 2.8491861030488508e-06, 0.0002564755850471556, 6.4