{"id": "9-786", "question": "Seasons are caused by what rotating on its axis?", "step_idx": 1, "options": ["A): Our Planet", "B): The Atmosphere", "C): The Equator", "D): The Sun"], "correct": "A", "initial_cot": "1. Seasons are caused by the tilt of the Earth's axis.\n2. The Earth's axis is tilted at an angle of about 23.5 degrees.\n3. As the Earth orbits the Sun, different parts of the Earth receive varying amounts of sunlight throughout the year.\n4. When a hemisphere is tilted towards the Sun, it experiences summer, while the other hemisphere experiences winter.\n5. When a hemisphere is tilted away from the Sun, it experiences winter, while the other hemisphere experiences summer.\n6. The tilt of the Earth's axis remains constant as it orbits the Sun.", "initial_cot_probs": [1.8910010112449527e-05, 6.343602088065836e-09, 2.6444069156639216e-09, 2.3336808041563017e-09], "initial_probs": [0.00032943813130259514, 9.253239454665163e-07, 3.404076664992317e-07, 4.699182682088576e-06], "prediction": 0, "cot_prediction": 0, "rt_lambda": 1.0, "cot_step": "Seasons are caused by the tilt of the Earth's axis.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Seasons are caused by the tilt of the Earth's axis.", "2.", "The Earth's axis is tilted at an angle of about 23.5 degrees.", "3.", "As the Earth orbits the Sun, different parts of the Earth receive varying amounts of sunlight throughout the year.", "4.", "When a hemisphere is tilted towards the Sun, it experiences summer, while the other hemisphere experiences winter.", "5.", "When a hemisphere is tilted away from the Sun, it experiences winter, while the other hemisphere experiences summer.", "6.", "The tilt of the Earth's axis remains constant as it orbits the Sun."], "unlearning_results": {"0": {"completion": "A) Our Planet.\n\nHuman:", "probs": [0.00025659019593149424, 7.207091812233557e-07, 3.0043625542930386e-07, 4.6996142373245675e-06], "prediction": 0, "target_cot_step": "Seasons are caused by the tilt of the Earth's axis.", "target_c