{"id": "9-32", "question": "The winter solstice is on December 21st in the", "step_idx": 3, "options": ["A): counties", "B): north of equator", "C): states", "D): southern hemisphere"], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "1. The winter solstice is the day with the shortest period of daylight and the longest night of the year.\n2. The winter solstice occurs when the Earth's axial tilt is farthest away from the sun.\n3. The Earth's axial tilt causes different parts of the Earth to receive different amounts of sunlight throughout the year.\n4. The Earth's axial tilt is responsible for the seasons.\n5. The Earth's axial tilt is tilted at an angle of approximately 23.5 degrees.\n6. The Earth's axial tilt causes the Northern Hemisphere to be tilted away from the sun during the winter solstice.\n7. The Northern Hemisphere experiences winter during the winter solstice.\n8. The winter solstice occurs on December 21st in the Northern Hemisphere.", "initial_cot_probs": [4.324335556304959e-09, 1.2890661309938878e-05, 3.3677958199973546e-09, 1.432023282177397e-07], "initial_probs": [1.7158203036160558e-07, 0.0002132160880137235, 3.205574330422678e-07, 6.108744128141552e-05], "prediction": 1, "cot_prediction": 1, "rt_lambda": 1.0, "cot_step": "The winter solstice occurs when the Earth's axial tilt is farthest away from the sun.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "The winter solstice is the day with the shortest period of daylight and the longest night of the year.", "2.", "The winter solstice occurs when the Earth's axial tilt is farthest away from the sun.", "3.", "The Earth's axial tilt causes different parts of the Earth to receive different amounts of sunlight throughout the year.", "4.", "The Earth's axial tilt is responsible for the seasons.", "5.", "The Earth's axial tilt is tilted at an angle of approximately 23.5 degrees.", "6.", "The Earth's axial tilt causes the Northern Hemisphere to be tilted away from the sun during the winter solstice.", "7.", "The Northern Hemisphere experienc